        "comments": "The assembly mMyoEma1.hap1.2 is based on 42x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds are named by synteny based on Myotis emarginatus (Geoffroy's bat) GCA_965115925.1. Chromosome X was identified through synteny analysis with Myotis daubentonii (GCA_963259705.1)The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 1 (99,058 - 104,530 Kbp) are unknown. The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 6 (97, 067 - 208.5 Kbp) are unknown. The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 1 (91.5 - 102,953 Kbp) are unknown.",
